.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH RANMA-CAPTURE 1 "" "ranma 0.1.0" "ranma manual"
.SH NAME
ranma\-capture \- Print a pane\*(Aqs text: its screen, and with \-\-history that many lines of scrollback above it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBranma capture\fR [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-pane\fR] [\fB\-H\fR|\fB\-\-history\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print a pane\*(Aqs text: its screen, and with \-\-history that many lines of scrollback above it
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-pane\fR \fI<PANE>\fR
The pane (from \fBranma panes\fR); the one this runs in when left out
.TP
\fB\-H\fR, \fB\-\-history\fR \fI<HISTORY>\fR [default: 0]
Lines of scrollback to print above the screen
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBranma\fR(1)
